  "source": "https://gc.nh.gov/rsa/html/LXIII/656/656-13.htm",
  "statuteText": "656:13 Questions on the Ballot. –\n\nExcept as provided in RSA 656:14, whenever a question is submitted to voters at a state general election as provided in RSA 663, the question shall be printed on the state general election ballot following the offices columns. Printed after the question there shall be 2 squares, boxes, ovals, or other appropriate symbol, one with the word \"yes\" beside it and another with the word \"no\" beside it."
